ational monuments through presidential proclamations under the Antiquities Act, requiring such regulation to continue under the Magnuson-Stevens Act instead.","summarySource":"ai","title":"To amend the Magnuson-Stevens Fishery Conservation and Management Act to provide for the regulation of fishing in marine national monuments.","type":"hr","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/8904"},{"bipartisan":false,"cosponsors":0,"crossPartyCosponsors":0,"id":"hr6158-119","introducedDate":"2025-11-19","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-11-19","text":"Referred to the House Committee on the Judiciary."},"number":"HR 6158","policyArea":"Immigration","ranked":true,"stage":"introduced","summary":"Amends immigration law to allow U.S. nationals born in American Samoa to elect citizenship by applying for a passport while residing in a U.S. state or territory, and repeals provisions regarding loss of nationality through residence abroad.","summarySource":"ai","title":"American Samoa Statutory Nationality and Citizenship Act","type":"hr","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/6158"},{"bipartisan":false,"cosponsors":0,"crossPartyCosponsors":0,"id":"hr5976-119","introducedDate":"2025-11-07","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-11-07","text":"Referred to the House Committee on the Judiciary."},"number":"HR 5976","policyArea":"Immigration","ranked":true,"stage":"introduced","summary":"Amends the Immigration and Nationality Act to allow U.S. nationals from American Samoa residing in a State or specified territory to apply for citizenship, and permits them to obtain passports identifying them as both nationals and citizens.","summarySource":"ai","title":"To protect collective self-determination and individual rights under Federal statutes conferring nationality on persons born and residing in the territory of American Samoa, to enable subsequent elective United States citizenship upon application of such persons residing in a State or in a territory subject to sections 301 through 308 of the Immigration and Nationality Act, and for other purposes.","type":"hr","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/5976"},{"bipartisan":true,"cosponsors":1,"crossPartyCosponsors":1,"id":"hr531-119","introducedDate":"2025-01-16","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-05-14","text":"Received in the Senate and Read twice and referred to the Committee on Commerce, Science, and Transportation."},"number":"HR 531","policyArea":"Public Lands and Natural Resources","ranked":true,"stage":"passed_one_chamber","summary":"South Pacific Tuna Treaty Act of 2025 This bill revises federal requirements for U.S. commercial fishing vessels operating in the South Pacific. The changes reflect amendments to the South Pacific Tuna Treaty that were agreed to at Nadi, Fiji, on December 3, 2016. The treaty details mutual obligations of the United States and 16 Pacific Island countries when U.S. fishing vessels operate in the...","summarySource":"crs","title":"South Pacific Tuna Treaty Act of 2025","type":"hr","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/531"},{"bipartisan":false,"cosponsors":0,"crossPartyCosponsors":0,"id":"hr449-119","introducedDate":"2025-01-15","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-01-15","text":"Referred to the House Committee on the Judiciary."},"number":"HR 449","policyArea":"Immigration","ranked":true,"stage":"introduced","summary":"This bill waives certain requirements for U.S. nationals applying for citizenship. Currently, individuals born in an outlying possession (i.e., American Samoa or Swains Island) are U.S. nationals but do not automatically acquire citizenship through birth in an outlying possession. Under this bill, a U.S. national who otherwise qualifies may become a citizen upon establishing residence and...","summarySource":"crs","title":"To amend the Immigration and Nationality Act to waive certain naturalization requirements for United States nationals, and for other purposes.","type":"hr","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/449"},{"bipartisan":false,"cosponsors":0,"crossPartyCosponsors":0,"id":"hr399-119","introducedDate":"2025-01-14","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-01-14","text":"Referred to the House Committee on Ways and Means."},"number":"HR 399","policyArea":"Taxation","ranked":true,"stage":"introduced","summary":"This bill permanently extends the American Samoa economic development tax credit, effective for tax years beginning after December 31, 2021. Under current law, certain qualified domestic corporations may be entitled to a tax credit for a percentage of qualified American Samoa wages, allocable employee fringe benefits, and depreciation allowances related to qualified American Samoa tangible...","summarySource":"crs","title":"To permanently extend the American Samoa economic development tax credit.","type":"hr","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/399"},{"bipartisan":false,"cosponsors":0,"crossPartyCosponsors":0,"id":"hr314-119","introducedDate":"2025-01-09","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-01-09","text":"Referred to the House Committee on Oversight and Government Reform."},"number":"HR 314","policyArea":"Government Operations and Politics","ranked":true,"stage":"introduced","summary":"Empowering Nonprofits Act This bill reduces cost-sharing requirements for grants directly awarded to certain nonprofit organizations for the five years following the bill's enactment. Eligible nonprofit organizations are those located in a U.S. state (including the District of Columbia or a U.S. commonwealth, territory, or possession) or federally recognized Indian tribe that has more than 20% of...","summarySource":"crs","title":"Empowering Nonprofits Act","type":"hr","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/314"},{"bipartisan":false,"cosponsors":0,"crossPartyCosponsors":0,"id":"hr315-119","introducedDate":"2025-01-09","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-01-10","text":"Referred to the Subcommittee on Economic Development, Public Buildings, and Emergency Management."},"number":"HR 315","policyArea":"Emergency Management","ranked":true,"stage":"introduced","summary":"This bill prohibits the Federal Emergency Management Agency from requiring the application of the Buy American requirements (requirements for the use of goods mined, produced, or manufactured in the United States) with respect to purchases made or contracts issued by Puerto Rico, the District of Columbia, American Samoa, or the U.S. Virgin Islands in the case of an emergency declaration.","summarySource":"crs","title":"To waive certain provisions in the case of an emergency declaration under the Robert T. Stafford Disaster Relief and Emergency Assistance Act.","type":"hr","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/315"}],"state":"AS","topCrossPartyCollaborators":[{"bioguideId":"C001055","caucus":"D","count":8,"name":"Ed Case"},{"bioguideId":"K000400","caucus":"D","count":4,"name":"Sydney Kamlager-Dove"},{"bioguideId":"B001287","caucus":"D","count":3,"name":"Ami Bera"},{"bioguideId":"M001241","caucus":"D","count":2,"name":"Dave Min"},{"bioguideId":"D000624","caucus":"D","count":2,"name":"Debbie Dingell"}]}
